+++ b/docs/PRIVACY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+Principles: collect the minimum, keep it first-party, be transparent next to
+the point of collection, and make the private choice the default so users
+don't have to do "privacy labor" (no consent banner is needed because nothing
+optional is collected).
+
+## 1. Third-party audit
+
+Last audit: 2026-11-13. Run `npm run audit:third-parties` for the static check
+(also suitable for CI). Repeat a runtime check on each release: load every
+page with DevTools → Network (or export a HAR) and confirm that every
+request goes to our own origin.
+
+| Resource | Before | Privacy risk | Decision |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Hero photo (`images.unsplash.com`) | Hotlinked from CSS | Every visitor's IP, UA and Referer sent to Unsplash/Imgix | **Self-hosted** at `/assets/img/hero.{webp,jpg}`, metadata stripped (photo from Unsplash, free licence) |
+| Fonts | System font stack | None | Keep. Do **not** add Google Fonts or similar; self-host fonts if needed |
+| Analytics / tag managers / pixels | None | — | Keep none. If ever needed: first-party, cookieless, aggregate-only, documented here first |
+| Social widgets / video embeds | None | — | Use plain share links and a click-to-load façade (`youtube-nocookie.com`) if ever added |
+
+**Rules for adding any third party:** document purpose, the data it receives
+and retention here; add it to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the audit script; pin a
+versioned URL with `integrity` + `crossorigin="anonymous"` +
+`referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`; update CSP/`Connection-Allowlist` in `_headers`
+and the meta CSP in `index.html`. Never load third parties on account,
+checkout or order pages.
+
+## 2. Data inventory (what the site collects)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Session identifier | `__Host-session` cookie | Keep the user signed in | Session; destroyed on logout |
+| Account & order details | Server (account pages) | Fulfil orders, rewards | While account is active; user can export/delete at `/account/privacy` |
+| Tracking params (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`, …) | — | Not used | Stripped from the URL client-side; must be dropped from server logs |
+
+The marketing pages set no cookies and use no web storage.
+
+## 3. What's implemented in this repo
+
+**Markup (`index.html`)**
+- No third-party resources; CSS/JS moved to same-origin files so CSP needs no `'unsafe-inline'`.
+- Meta CSP + `<meta name="referrer">` as a fallback for hosts that can't set headers.
+- Logout is a `POST` form (not a GET link): it can't be triggered by link
+  prefetchers or cross-site `<img>` requests, and its response can carry `Clear-Site-Data`.
+- A plain-language privacy statement in the footer, linking to data export/deletion.
+
+**Client script (`js/privacy.js`)**: strips tracking parameters from the
+address bar, shows when Global Privacy Control is detected and honoured, and
+clears web storage when the user logs out. It uses no fingerprinting APIs and
+writes to the DOM only with `textContent`.
+
+**Headers (`_headers`)**: strict CSP (`default-src 'none'`, self-only,
+Trusted Types, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, reporting), `Connection-Allowlist`
+(self-only), `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, a deny-by-default
+`Permissions-Policy` (including ad/topics/attribution APIs), COOP/CORP,
+`nosniff`, HSTS (ramp-up), `Cache-Control: no-store` on personal pages, and
+`Clear-Site-Data` on `/logout`. `npm start` serves the CSP locally via `statikk --csp`.
+
+## 4. Server-side requirements (outside this static repo)
+
+- Session cookie: `Set-Cookie: __Host-session=…; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+- `POST /logout`: invalidate the session server-side, respond with
+  `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"`, then `303` to `/`.
+  Reject `GET /logout`.
+- `/api/reports/*`: accept Reporting API payloads and strip query strings, tokens
+  and IP addresses before storing them; keep reports for 30 days at most.
+- Access logs: drop or truncate IP addresses, and remove query strings and tracking parameters; rotate them quickly.
+- Treat `Sec-GPC: 1` as an opt-out of any sale or sharing of data.
+- Rate-limit account and lookup endpoints so data can't be scraped in bulk.
+- `/account/privacy`: self-service data export, correction and deletion, as easy as sign-up.
+- Forms: ask only for required fields, use the coarsest granularity (e.g. birthday month for rewards, not full DOB),
+  and explain inline why each field is requested.
